        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c6452b5596ae4c848f9668efefdc572b",
      "statement": "ScoringQueue.submit catches TaskRejectedException from the bounded executor, removes the rejected article id from its in-flight set, and relies on the periodic sweep to re-enqueue it later; this is why the executor deliberately keeps the default abort rejection policy rather than a discarding policy, which would otherwise leave the id marked in-flight forever.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/service/ScoringQueue.java#L52-L72",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:de729a69c86852371b9328141c76e0e8d4b991f07623f199fbc7e57c7bc2e821:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bd01705a1aba4861a6d34ffffede9869",
      "statement": "myfeeder.interest.concurrency stays at 1 for rate-limit safety against Jev's per-account request rate, and this concurrency limit together with the single Resilience4j retry layer is the whole rate-limit safety mechanism; raising concurrency or re-adding SDK retries would each independently defeat it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L237-L242",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:541f32056b5f0ac046b68e78ff8e533376fbc541fffb3573c831091e4a84e58e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/config/InterestScoringConfig.java#L15-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28c8c04d3bdd514526d09242b447ec80777ae9230290a31a2fe46dc27b1d7945:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b20a2df49ab44a7597496d2880d6a959",
      "statement": "The operational throttle levers for Jev rate-limiting are, in order: a release change lowering myfeeder.interest.sweep-batch-size and/or lengthening myfeeder.interest.sweep-delay in application.yaml; or an emergency `kubectl -n myfeeder set env deploy/myfeeder MYFEEDER_INTEREST_SWEEPBATCHSIZE=<n>` override (relaxed-binding env name for sweep-batch-size) that restarts the pod immediately and must be removed explicitly with `kubectl ... MYFEEDER_INTEREST_SWEEPBATCHSIZE-` once encoded into yaml, because a Helm upgrade's three-way merge can otherwise keep an out-of-band env var across deploys.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L242-L242",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2792cc3857e708588bbbe94a695c3f120984037c59b9c4b418be1c7966aa998a:"
